# ─── VaultBot configuration ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your values. See the README for setup.

# ─── Vault path ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The absolute path to your Obsidian vault (this repo's root by default).
VAULT_PATH=.

# ─── Owner identity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your name. VaultBot addresses you by this and treats you as its operator.
# Leave blank to have VaultBot call you "the user" until it learns your name.
VAULTBOT_OWNER=

# ─── Ollama (embeddings always; LLM optional) ───────────────────────────────
# Ollama runs locally. The setup script auto-pulls the embedding + small models:
#   1. nomic-embed-text (~270 MB) — the embedding model (always local)
#   2. qwen3.5:4b (~4 GB) — the SMALL model for classification/routing
#      (set below; auto-pulled by the installer)
# The BIG chat/synthesis model is NOT auto-pulled — you choose it below.
#
# Two ways to provide the big chat model:
#   1. Local Ollama (DEFAULT, zero-config): manually run
#      `ollama pull <model>` after setup. Embeddings already use Ollama
#      so this adds no new dependency. Works offline, free, private.
#   2. Cloud API (RECOMMENDED for laptops): set LLM_BACKEND=openai below
#      + LLM_API_KEY + LLM_MODEL. Zero local compute, works on any laptop.
#      Free-tier OpenRouter models work great (see openrouter.ai/models).
#
# Embeddings ALWAYS use Ollama + nomic-embed-text (light, ~270 MB).
OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_LLM_MODEL=
OLLAMA_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text

# ─── Model preloading (reduces first-chat TTFT for local models) ──────────
# Ollama loads models lazily; the first request to a cold model can take
# minutes for large models (27B+). Preloading forces the model into GPU
# memory BEFORE the user's first message, so TTFT is just inference, not
# load + inference.
# VAULTBOT_OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE: how long Ollama keeps the model resident after
#   the last request (Ollama duration: "30m", "2h", "-1" forever, "0" evict).
#   Default "30m". Sent with every chat/generate/embedding call.
# VAULTBOT_PRELOAD_ON_STARTUP: preload models when the backend starts (1/0).
#   Default 1. Runs in a background thread; the server accepts connections
#   immediately while the model loads.
# VAULTBOT_PRELOAD_ON_CONNECT: preload when a chat WebSocket opens (1/0).
#   Default 1. Skips if the model is already resident. No-op for cloud.
#VAULTBOT_OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=30m
#VAULTBOT_PRELOAD_ON_STARTUP=1
#VAULTBOT_PRELOAD_ON_CONNECT=1

# ─── Chat / synthesis LLM backend ──────────────────────────────────────────
# LLM_BACKEND=ollama  -> (DEFAULT, zero-config) use local Ollama for chat.
#   Requires `ollama pull <model>` after setup (the installer does NOT
#   auto-pull chat models — only the lightweight embedding model).
# LLM_BACKEND=openai  -> use any OpenAI-compatible cloud API (recommended for
#   laptops: zero local compute). Set LLM_API_KEY + LLM_MODEL + LLM_BASE_URL.
#   Examples: OpenAI (gpt-4o-mini), OpenRouter (any model), vLLM, LM Studio.
#
# If LLM_BACKEND=openai but LLM_API_KEY is empty/missing, the backend
# fails with a clear error. Set the key to actually use the cloud backend.
LLM_BACKEND=ollama
LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# ─── Vision model (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# A vision-capable model for reading textbook pages with figures/equations.
# Can be local Ollama or cloud (same backend selection as the chat model).
# If unset, the chat model's own vision capability is used as fallback.
# Procedures with model_cartridge: vision delegate to this model.
VISION_MODEL=

# ─── Small model — the tiny local dance partner ──────────────────────────
# A small LOCAL-ONLY Ollama model (qwen3.5:4b, ~4 GB) that procedures can
# delegate to for cheap classification, tagging, and routing. The small
# model still needs to do real work, so it shouldn't be smaller than ~3-4B
# — sub-1B models (like the old qwen3.5:0.8b) can't reliably classify or
# route. The installer pulls it automatically. Runs on any laptop, costs
# zero cloud tokens. As more procedures use the small cartridge, the big
# cloud model does less and less.
# If unset, procedures requesting the small cartridge fall back to the big model.
SMALL_MODEL=qwen3.5:4b

# ─── Research backend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "freesearch" (default, keyless: DuckDuckGo + Marginalia + arXiv) or
# "tavily" (API-key'd, no rate-limiting, returns content inline).
VAULTBOT_RESEARCH_BACKEND=freesearch
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# ─── SearXNG (optional self-hosted search, needs Docker) ───────────────────
# If Docker is installed, the setup script automatically starts a SearXNG
# container that joins the FreeSearch pool for mainstream-web coverage
# (Google, Brave, DuckDuckGo via one private instance). Without Docker,
# the keyless backends (DDG Lite, Marginalia, arXiv) still work but are
# more rate-limited.
SEARXNG_PORT=8080

# ─── Community contributions (opt-in) ─────────────────────────────────────
# VaultBot can give back to the community: file issues when it hits an
# obstacle it was already solving, and (when you ask) submit a pull request.
# This is OFF by default — VaultBot is pull-only and will never write to
# GitHub (not even an issue) without your explicit permission.
#
# Authentication is handled by the GitHub CLI (`gh`), NOT a token here:
#   gh auth login
# The installer runs this for you. The contribution tools
# (submit_contribution, review_contributions, torture_test, github_issues)
# shell out to `gh`, so you never manage a personal access token by hand.
#
# VAULTBOT_ALLOW_CONTRIBUTIONS: set to "true" to opt in. The plugin's
# "Allow contributions" setting writes this automatically.
#VAULTBOT_ALLOW_CONTRIBUTIONS=false
#
# VAULTBOT_GH_BOT_USER: the GitHub account your VaultBot authors PRs as.
# Only the maintainer's community VaultBot needs this — it lets the bot
# author PRs as a separate account (e.g. "ziggibot-uni") so the human
# maintainer can approve them (GitHub forbids approving your own PR).
# Everyone else's VaultBot just uses whatever account `gh auth login`
# signed into. Leave unset unless you are the maintainer.
#VAULTBOT_GH_BOT_USER=